Rules for frontend development:

- The local frontend is always running on localhost:3000
- Always prefer building stuff with Nuxt UI Components over normal html tags
- Always use the Nuxt Docs to check for existing components before implementing anything. ('https://ui3.nuxt.com/components). You can use the playwright mcp to help as well.
- Always use the playwright MCP as you code to test out changes. When everything is working and validated, write an e2e spec for the changes.
- Always make sure that things are smooth - animations and transitions should be a default.
- Transitions should be centralized at assets/css/transitions.css
- Animations should use v-auto-animate whenever possible (module already setup). Use the docs https://auto-animate.formkit.com/#usage-vue for reference
- Always use brazilian portuguese for all text.
- Always use <script setup lang="ts"> for the script blocks in vue components
- For testing on the frontend, you can use the credentials email guima+bloodbank@hemocione.com.br and password hemocione123
- Use Yarn
- Api routes should use the /v1/ prefix and only call services.
- Services can call the mongoose models to make queries.
- ONLY LIGHT MODE SUPPORT. DONT SUPPORT DARK MODE.
- Use NuxtImg instead of normal img tags.
- Use fetchWithAuth instead of $fetch (unless user used $fetch manually)
- Use useFetchWithAuth instead of useFetch (unless user used useFetch manually)
- For Map stuff, use the docs at https://indoorequal.github.io/vue-maplibre-gl/api/
- For generic errors, use the useToast from NuxtUI (https://ui3.nuxt.com/composables/use-toast)
- Prefer the bloodBanksLocationId for querying
- Prefer tailwind for css styling
- Use the mongodb mcp for validating data in the DB
